/**
 * Taiwan's counties/cities and townships/districts with their English names,
 * for the herbarium label's Loc. line. Data, not logic — generated once from
 * the two official sources below; do not edit by hand.
 *
 * Township/district English is TONGYONG PINYIN, taken verbatim from the
 * Ministry of the Interior's 「臺灣地區鄉鎮市區級以上行政區域名稱中英對照表」
 * (author LAND.MOI, file dated 2004-01, the Tongyong-era table;
 * copy: rootlaw.com.tw A040040091067000-0980224-12000-001.doc). That table
 * predates the 2010/2014 mergers, so each current district was matched to its
 * 2004 township by name within its predecessor county (新北市←臺北縣;
 * 臺中／臺南／高雄 county + city; 桃園縣→桃園市) and given the suffix of its
 * current type (區 District, 鄉／鎮 Township, 市 City). Three are not in the
 * 2004 table:
 *   - 那瑪夏區 (formerly 三民鄉): "Namasia", the district office's
 *     own English name (namasia-en.kcg.gov.tw), from the indigenous name;
 *   - 東沙群島 / 南沙群島: Dongsha / Nansha, spelled the same in both systems.
 *
 * County/city English is the conventional form both tables use (Taipei,
 * Kaohsiung, …), per Chunghwa Post's 縣市鄉鎮中英對照檔 (County_h_10906.xml,
 * data.gov.tw dataset 5949). Its township names are HANYU pinyin and appear
 * here only as `hanyu`, a matching key for a geocoder answering in English —
 * never printed.
 */
export type TwDistrict = {
  county: string;
  district: string;
  /** Tongyong pinyin, with the current type suffix. */
  tongyong: string;
  /** Hanyu pinyin (Chunghwa Post) — for matching only. */
  hanyu: string;
};

